<node id="11104736" title="Re^6: Perl 6 to be renamed?" created="2019-08-20 10:54:26" updated="2019-08-20 10:54:26" _doctext_mode="lenient"><type id="11">note</type>
<author id="170442">jdporter</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;i&gt;
There is no "Perl6". Read the news. 
&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
Did I miss something?  The latest I read was that they were considering adding an "alias" to the branding (essentially)... but &lt;i&gt;not&lt;/i&gt; abandoning the "Perl 6" name. So the outward marketing can be more sane, while the unpleasantness within the community can continue raging.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
Now, if you're referring to the fact that &lt;tt&gt;@lwall&lt;/tt&gt; has declaimed very clearly that the name is "Perl 6, with a space" and not "Perl6", then yes... but that's not news.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="pmsig"&gt;&lt;div class="pmsig-170442"&gt;
I reckon we are the only monastery ever to have a dungeon stuffed with 16[523120|,]000 zombies.
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</doctext>
